cliffordModule -- makes a clifford Module
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        M = cliffordModule(M1,M2,R)
        M = cliffordModule(eOdd,eEv)
  * Inputs:
      * M1, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
      * M2, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, M1, M2 a matrix
        factorization of a quadratic form qq
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, base ring of the quadratic form
      * eEv, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, 
      * eOdd, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, lists such as the output of
        cliffordOperators(M1,M2)
  * Outputs:
      * M, an instance of the type *note CliffordModule: CliffordModule,, 

Description
===========

The keys oddOperators evenOperators are the same as the two lists output by
cliffordOperators(M1,M2)

The keys evenCenter oddCenter yield the action of the center of the even
Clifford algebra of qq on the even, respectively odd parts of the Clifford
module.

The key symmetricM yields the matrix of coefficients of the quadratic form qq

the key hyperellipticBranchEquation yields the branch equation in R -- that is,
the equation of the set of points over which the quadratic form is singular.

+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : kk = ZZ/101                                              |
|                                                              |
|o1 = kk                                                       |
|                                                              |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                             |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : setRandomSeed 0                                          |
| -- setting random seed to 0                                  |
|                                                              |
|o2 = 0                                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : g = 1                                                    |
|                                                              |
|o3 = 1                                                        |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : (S, qq,  R,  u, M1, M2, Mu1, Mu2)=randomNicePencil(kk,g);|
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : M = cliffordModule(M1,M2, R)                             |
|                                                              |
|o5 = CliffordModule{...6...}                                  |
|                                                              |
|o5 : CliffordModule                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : Mu = cliffordModule(Mu1,Mu2, R)                          |
|                                                              |
|o6 = CliffordModule{...6...}                                  |
|                                                              |
|o6 : CliffordModule                                           |
+--------------------------------------------------------------+

The symmetric matrices are the same for both:

+------------------------------+
|i7 : Mu.symmetricM            |
|                              |
|o7 = | -5t  -50s 6t     -6t  ||
|     | -50s 0    -9t    5t   ||
|     | 6t   -9t  -s-30t 3t   ||
|     | -6t  5t   3t     -48t ||
|                              |
|             4      4         |
|o7 : Matrix R  <-- R          |
+------------------------------+
|i8 : M.symmetricM             |
|                              |
|o8 = | -5t  -50s 6t     -6t  ||
|     | -50s 0    -9t    5t   ||
|     | 6t   -9t  -s-30t 3t   ||
|     | -6t  5t   3t     -48t ||
|                              |
|             4      4         |
|o8 : Matrix R  <-- R          |
+------------------------------+

But the operators are twice the size for M (in both cases the same size as the
corresponding matrix factorization Mu.evenCenter numrows(Mu.evenCenter) ==
numrows(Mu1) M.evenCenter

