orderInPic -- order of a line bundle of degree 0 in Pic(E)
**********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        N = orderInPic(L)
        N = orderInPic(phi)
  * Inputs:
      * L, an instance of the type *note VectorBundleOnE: VectorBundleOnE,, a
        line bundle of degree 0 on E
      * phi, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a matrix which is the
        yAction of VectorBundleOnE
  * Outputs:
      * N, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, the order of L in Pic(E)

Description
===========

Computes the order of a degree 0 line bundle L on the hyperelliptic curve E by
the most naive method.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : setRandomSeed 0                                                         |
| -- setting random seed to 0                                                 |
|                                                                             |
|o1 = 0                                                                       |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : kk=ZZ/101;                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : g=1;                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : rNP=randNicePencil(kk,g);                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : f=(cliffordModule(rNP.matFact1,rNP.matFact2,rNP.baseRing)).             |
|                                                                             |
|          3       2 2        3      4                                        |
|o5 = - 12s t - 50s t  - 16s*t  + 47t                                         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : kk[s, t]                                                                |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|hyperellipticBranchEquation                                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : L=randomLineBundle(0,f);                                                |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : orderInPic L                                                            |
|                                                                             |
|o7 = 37                                                                      |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

The ground field kk has to be finite. It computes the order by checking
inductively whether L^k is trivial, so it may fail when kk is not finite, or
has too many elements. orderInPic(phi) may not terminate if it is not the
yAction of a line bundle of degree 0 on E.

See also
========

  * *note randomLineBundle: randomLineBundle, -- a random balanced line bundle
    on the hyperelliptic curve
  * *note vectorBundleOnE: vectorBundleOnE, -- creates a VectorBundleOnE,
    represented as a matrix factorization
  * *note VectorBundleOnE: VectorBundleOnE, -- vector bundle on a hyperelliptic
    curve E
  * *note yAction: yAction, -- defines a vector bundle on E

Ways to use orderInPic:
=======================

