tensorProduct -- tensor product of sheaves on the elliptic curve or sheaf times CliffordModule
**********************************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        eta = tensorProduct(phi,psi)
        G = tensorProduct(M,V)
        L = tensorProduct(L1,L2)
  * Inputs:
      * phi, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, 
      * psi, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, representing the action of
        y on a sheaf on PP^1
      * L1, an instance of the type *note VectorBundleOnE: VectorBundleOnE,, 
      * L2, an instance of the type *note VectorBundleOnE: VectorBundleOnE,, 
      * M, an instance of the type *note CliffordModule: CliffordModule,, 
      * V, an instance of the type *note VectorBundleOnE: VectorBundleOnE,, 
  * Outputs:
      * eta, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, action of y
      * N, an instance of the type *note CliffordModule: CliffordModule,, 
      * L, an instance of the type *note VectorBundleOnE: VectorBundleOnE,, 

Description
===========

Sheaves on the hyperelliptic curve y^2 -(-1)^{g}* f(s,t) are represented as
sheaves on PP^1 together with the action of y. Clifford modules are represented
as the action of maps eOdd_i: M_1 \to M_0 and eEv_i:M_0 \to M_1 between the
even and odd parts of the module. The result are the corresponding data for the
tensor product.





